   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Two part question.</div><div><br></div><div>First, what is this  &quot;printSamplersByType(ind) : something went wrong&quot; error message mean? Has anyone seen this pop up during the \r\nconfigureMCMC step?<br></div><div><br></div><div>And second, I wanted to double check that using [print = FALSE] in the configureMCMC step to bypass this error message isn&#39;t masking a critical problem with the model. <br></div><div><br></div><div>The rest of the model superficially seems &#39;fine&#39;. All parameters are initialized, log-likelihood can be calculated, the model runs when the error message is silenced, and the resulting chains seem to be acting normally and converge. I can&#39;t easily provide a reproducible example on the listserv since I am not sure what the issue is and the model is, for a lack of a better word, convoluted, but I can send the model code off-line if a deeper dive is necessary.  My initial thought was there was an  issue with the naming of parameters that need samplers in the model, or the sheer number of them, but that is just wild speculation.<br></div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;ma