   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dan, thanks for raising this issue, and also sending your example off-list.<div><br></div><div>For anyone interested, the problem was stemming from using *both* variable names &quot;x_y&quot; and also &quot;x.y&quot; in model code.  This won&#39;t cause any problems with the nimble model object, or the correct execution of the MCMC.  But, the regular expressions being used in printSamplersByType were interpreting the &quot;.&quot; as a regular expression wildcard, and thus matching variable names incorrectly.</div><div><br></div><div>A patch is available on the development branch of nimble.  Until the next release, this can be installed and used as:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">remove.packages(&#39;nimble&#39;)<br>library(remotes)<br>remotes::install_github(&#39;nimble-dev/nimble&#39;, ref = &#39;devel&#39;, subdir = &#39;packages/nimble&#39;)<br>library(nimble)</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Daniel</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Mar 24, 2023 at 2:16 PM Daniel Turek &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danie...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dan, thanks for emailing.<div><br></div><div>There is almost certainly no deeper underlying problem with your model (given everything else you reported).  With practical certainty this is some overlooked case in the printSamplersByType method.  And the unhelpful error message is entirely on me - apologies.</div><div><br></div><div>Can you please send a reproducible example to me, off list?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Daniel</div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Mar 24, 2023 at 1:34 PM <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gib...@vt.edu</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gib...@vt.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Two part question.</div><div><br></div><div>First, what is this  &quot;printSamplersByType(ind) : something went wrong&quot; error message mean? Has anyone seen this pop up during the \r\nconfigureMCMC step?<br></div><div><br></div><div>And second, I wanted to double check that using [print = FALSE] in the configureMCMC step to bypass this error message isn&#39;t masking a critical problem with the model. <br></div><div><br></div><div>The rest of the model superficially seems &#39;fine&#39;. All parameters are initialized, log-likelihood can be calculated, the model runs when the error message is silenced, and the resulting chains seem to be acting normally and converge. I can&#39;t easily provide a reproducible example on the listserv since I am not sure wha